---
import ArticleLayout from "../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";

const title = "BC PNP Questions Answered (2026): 38 Quick Answers From an RCIC";
const description = "Direct, current answers to 38 of the most-searched BC PNP questions: eligibility, job offers, points, draws, fees, processing times, applying and special cases.";
const canonical = "https://bcpnpcalculator.ca/articles/bc-pnp-questions-answered";

const linkClass = "text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline";

const groups = [
  {
    id: "basics",
    title: "BC PNP Basics",
    intro: "Start here if you are new to the program. These answers explain what the BC PNP is, how big it is and how competitive it has become in 2026.",
    items: [
      {
        q: "What is the BC PNP?",
        a: "The BC Provincial Nominee Program (BC PNP) is British Columbia's economic immigration program. The province selects workers and entrepreneurs it needs and nominates them to Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada (IRCC) for permanent residence. A nomination is not permanent residence itself: you still apply to IRCC, which makes the final decision after medical, security and criminality checks. The BC PNP has two parts: Skills Immigration, for workers with a B.C. job offer, and Entrepreneur Immigration, for people who start or buy a business. Whether you search for BC PNP, PNP BC or the BC PNP program in Canada, it is the same program, run by the B.C. government through WelcomeBC. For 2026, IRCC gave B.C. 6,254 nominations.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/what-is-pnp-provincial-nominee-program", label: "What is the Provincial Nominee Program?" }],
      },
      {
        q: "How does the BC PNP work?",
        a: "For most workers it is a four-step process. First, you get a qualifying job offer from an eligible B.C. employer. Second, you submit a free registration online, which scores you out of 200 points on your job offer, wage, work location, experience, education and language. Third, B.C. holds draws and invites the top scorers in targeted groups; once invited, you have 30 calendar days to submit a complete application with a $1,750 fee. Fourth, if the BC PNP approves it, you are nominated and apply to IRCC for permanent residence. Health Authority stream candidates skip the registration and draw and apply directly.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/how-to-apply-bc-pnp", label: "How to apply for the BC PNP, step by step" }],
      },
      {
        q: "What is BC PNP Express Entry (Express Entry BC)?",
        a: "Express Entry BC (EEBC) is an option inside the Skilled Worker and Health Authority streams, not a separate set of rules. If you also qualify for a federal Express Entry program (Federal Skilled Worker, Canadian Experience Class or Federal Skilled Trades) and have an active Express Entry profile, you link it to your BC PNP file. A nomination then adds 600 points to your Comprehensive Ranking System (CRS) score; in 2026, IRCC's provincial nominee rounds had lowest scores between 697 and 805. Your permanent residence application is then processed through Express Entry, which has a six-month service standard. Note that IRCC announced on October 16, 2026 a CRS overhaul taking effect November 3, 2026; the announcement does not mention the nomination points.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/bc-pnp-express-entry-bc-eebc-guide-2026", label: "Express Entry BC guide" }],
      },
      {
        q: "How many people get BC PNP each year?",
        a: "The number is capped by an annual allocation from IRCC. For 2026, B.C. was first given 5,254 nominations in December 2025, and IRCC added 1,000 more on August 18, 2026, for a total of 6,254. B.C. says it intends to use the full allocation by December 31, 2026. For comparison, the BC PNP nominated 6,214 people in 2025 after two mid-year top-ups, 8,000 in 2024 and 8,200 in 2023. Invitations are not the same as nominations: from February 4 to October 8, 2026, B.C. issued at least 6,297 Skills Immigration invitations, but some invited people never apply and some applications are refused.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/bc-pnp-statistical-report-2025-analysis", label: "BC PNP Statistical Report 2025, explained" }],
      },
      {
        q: "Is it easy to get BC PNP?",
        a: "No. It is achievable for the right profile, but it is competitive and narrower than it was a few years ago. You need a job offer from an eligible B.C. employer, and 12 occupations, including administrative assistants, bookkeepers and retail and food service supervisors, cannot be nominated at all for applications submitted after June 13, 2026. On October 6, 2026 there were 7,695 registrations in the pool, and about 71% scored below 110. Your occupation now matters as much as your score: health workers were invited at 76 points in September and October 2026, while candidates outside the Care and Build lists needed 131 points or a wage of at least $52 an hour and $105,000 a year.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/bc-pnp-2026-draws-recap-2027-forecast", label: "Every 2026 draw, with trends" }],
      },
      {
        q: "When will the BC PNP reopen?",
        a: "The BC PNP never fully closed, but several doors have shut. In 2025, with an initial allocation of 4,000, B.C. held only three Skills Immigration rounds and focused intake on health care and high-economic-impact workers. The International Graduate stream closed in November 2024 and the International Post-Graduate stream in January 2025. Planned bachelor's, master's and doctorate streams were suspended in April 2025, and on April 23, 2026 B.C. said it will not launch new student streams. The same update closed the Entry Level and Semi-Skilled stream and confirmed tech draws had ended. As of October 2026, the Skilled Worker and Health Authority streams (with the Express Entry BC option) and Entrepreneur Immigration are open.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/bc-pnp-2027-outlook-predictions", label: "BC PNP 2027 outlook" }],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "eligibility",
    title: "Eligibility and Job Offers",
    intro: "In 2026, eligibility starts with the job offer and the employer. These answers summarize the Skills Immigration Program Guide in force since mid-2026.",
