      {
        q: "How many points are required for the BC PNP?",
        a: "There is no fixed pass mark. Each draw sets its own minimum, depending on how many people B.C. wants to invite from a group and how many registrants that group has. On October 8, 2026 the minimums were 76 for Care: Health, 99 for Care: Childcare, 94 for Build: Construction Trades and 86 for Veterinary Care. The most recent Innovate (High Economic Impact) round, on September 24, 2026, needed 131 points, or a wage of at least $52 an hour and $105,000 a year in a TEER 0 to 3 job. Each category opened higher earlier in 2026, from 100 (Veterinary, May) to 138 (Innovate, February and April).",
        links: [
          { href: "/bc-pnp-draws", label: "Latest BC PNP draws" },
