        q: "What is regional experience in the BC PNP?",
        a: "It is a 10-point bonus within the area of employment factor, and it only applies if your job offer is outside Metro Vancouver. Under section 8.5 of the program guide, Area 1 (Metro Vancouver) earns 0 points, Area 2 (Squamish, Abbotsford, Agassiz, Mission and Chilliwack) earns 5, and Area 3 (the rest of B.C.) earns 15. If your job is in Area 2 or 3, you get 10 more for regional experience, meaning at least one year of full-time paid work in Area 2 or 3 within the five years before you register, or for being a recent graduate of a public institution outside Metro Vancouver. You can claim only one, so the area maximum is 25.",
        links: [{ href: "/articles/bc-pnp-look-west-regional-nominations-2027", label: "Regional points and the 35% goal" }],
