        q: "What is an eligible professional designation in the BC PNP?",
        a: "It is a 5-point bonus in the education factor for holding a B.C. professional designation linked to your job offer. Section 8.2 of the program guide lists which ones count. They include health care assistants on the BC Care Aide and Community Health Worker Registry, practical nurses licensed with BCCNM, early childhood educators with a One Year or Five Year certificate (not Assistant), dental hygienists and dental technicians registered with the BC College of Oral Health Professionals, licensed traditional Chinese medicine practitioners and acupuncturists, veterinary technicians registered with the BC Veterinary Technologists Association, and trades workers with a valid SkilledTradesBC certificate or registered apprenticeship. Not every regulated profession is listed; veterinarians, for example, are not.",
