<ArticleLayout slug="bc-pnp-questions-answered" datePublished="2026-10-18" dateModified="2026-10-18" articleSection="Guide" keywords="BC PNP questions, what is BC PNP, how does BC PNP work, BC PNP requirements, BC PNP points required, next BC PNP draw, how long does BC PNP take, BC PNP cost, how to apply for BC PNP, BC PNP Express Entry, BC PNP tech pilot, BC PNP international graduate" title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="inline-block bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-800 px-4 py-1 rounded-full text-sm font-bold mb-4 border border-indigo-200 shadow-sm">
        FAQ Hub
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        BC PNP Questions Answered (2026): 38 Quick Answers From an RCIC
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-4">
        Short, direct answers to the questions people search most about British Columbia's Provincial Nominee Program, each checked against the October 2026 rules and linked to our full guide on the topic.
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <time datetime="2026-10-18">October 18, 2026</time>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <span>20 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 p-6 mb-10 rounded-r-xl">
      <p class="font-semibold text-emerald-900 mb-2">Quick answer</p>
      <p class="text-emerald-800">
        The BC PNP is British Columbia's program for nominating workers and entrepreneurs for Canadian permanent residence. In 2026 it has 6,254 nominations and, for workers, requires a job offer from an eligible B.C. employer. Registrations are scored out of 200, and draw minimums in September and October 2026 ranged from 76 (health occupations) to 131 (High Economic Impact). The application fee is $1,750, and IRCC fees and processing come after nomination.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-2xl text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-black text-indigo-600 mb-2">6,254</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 font-medium">BC PNP nominations for 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-2xl text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-black text-green-600 mb-2">7,695</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 font-medium">Registrations in the pool, Oct 6, 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-2xl text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-black text-red-600 mb-2">76–131</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 font-medium">Draw minimums, Sep–Oct 2026</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed">
        Most BC PNP questions have short answers that are easy to get wrong, because the program changed more in 2025 and 2026 than in the previous decade. Tech draws ended, student streams closed, a list of ineligible occupations arrived, and draws now target Care, Build and Innovate priorities. This hub answers 38 of the most common questions in 60 to 150 words each, grouped by theme. Each answer ends with a link to our in-depth article if you need more. To see where your own profile stands, use the <a href="/bc-pnp-calculator" class="text-indigo-600 underline font-semibold">BC PNP calculator</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="text-base text-gray-500">
        This is general information, not legal advice. Your situation may turn on details that a short answer cannot cover.
      </p>

      <nav class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Jump to a section</p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-1 text-base">
          <li><a href="#at-a-glance" class={linkClass}>BC PNP at a glance (October 2026)</a></li>
          {groups.map((g) => (
            <li><a href={`#${g.id}`} class={linkClass}>{g.title}</a> <span class="text-slate-500">({g.items.length} questions)</span></li>
          ))}
          <li><a href="#sources" class={linkClass}>Sources</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="at-a-glance" class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6 scroll-mt-24">BC PNP at a Glance (October 2026)</h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
        <table class="min-w-full border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-700">Topic</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-700">Status as of October 18, 2026</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">2026 allocation</td><td class="px-4 py-3">6,254 (5,254 announced December 2025, plus 1,000 on August 18, 2026)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Open streams</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Skilled Worker and Health Authority (each with the Express Entry BC option); Entrepreneur Immigration Base and Regional</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Closed or ended</td><td class="px-4 py-3">International Graduate (Nov 2024), International Post-Graduate (Jan 2025), Entry Level and Semi-Skilled (Apr 2026), priority tech draws (last held Dec 3, 2024)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Draw types</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Care (health, childcare, education, veterinary), Build (construction trades), Innovate (High Economic Impact by wage or score)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Latest draws</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Oct 8: Health 76, Childcare 99, Construction 94, Veterinary 86. Sep 24 Innovate: 131 points, or $52/hr and $105,000/yr</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Job offer</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Required for Skills Immigration; 12 occupations ineligible for applications after June 13, 2026</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Fees</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Registration free; application $1,750; IRCC $1,590 per adult (including the $600 RPRF)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Key deadlines</td><td class="px-4 py-3">30 calendar days to apply after an invitation; registrations expire after 12 months</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {groups.map((g) => (
        <section>
          <h2 id={g.id} class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6 scroll-mt-24">{g.title}</h2>
          <p>{g.intro}</p>

          {g.id === "points" && (
            <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
              <table class="min-w-full border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                <thead class="bg-slate-100">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-700">Factor</th>
